proofs.proof_tex:
For each \(j\geq1\), set \(k=j\), \(\varepsilon_j=2^{-j}\), and use the effective normalized Airy-record lemma to generate the complete verified record.  Apply the uniform face-robust Bayes-expansion lemma with tolerance \(2^{-j}\).  Increase its computable threshold, if necessary, until it also certifies the corrected positivity inequality, the rational Airy eigenvalue bracket has width at most \(2^{-j}\), and the primal bound from the rational-grid lemma obeys
\[
 (B_{c^\dagger}+1/4)n^{-1/6}+2^{-n}\leq2^{-j}.
 \tag{33}
\]
Call the resulting strictly increasing computable thresholds \(N_j\).  On input \(n\), choose
\[
 k_n=\max\{j\leq n:N_j\leq n\},
 \qquad \varepsilon_n^{\mathrm A}=2^{-k_n},             \tag{34}
\]
using a harmless fixed output on the finite prefix where the set is empty.  Since every \(N_j\) is finite, (34) is nondecreasing and tends to infinity; hence \(\varepsilon_n^{\mathrm A}\) is nonincreasing and tends to zero.  The threshold construction gives
\(\alpha_n(3T_{k_n}^\dagger+4\varepsilon_n^{\mathrm A})\leq1\).

Run finite-input mode of the corrected evaluator with enclosure width \(2^{-n}\).  The face-robust fixed-input evaluator lemma proves termination and returns the exact three stratum maxima.  Define each of \(e_{\mathrm{loc},n}\), \(e_{\mathrm{shell},n}\), and \(e_{\mathrm{zero},n}\) to be the rational outward enclosure of the positive part of its corresponding maximum minus the rational lower endpoint for \(\Lambda_{c^\dagger}\), enlarged by the eigenvalue-bracket width.  The uniform Bayes-expansion lemma and
\[
 \mathcal E_{j,2^{-j}}
 \leq\Lambda_{c^\dagger}+2^{-j}+\frac{15}{256}2^{-j}
 \tag{35}
\]
then certify all three inequalities in (A), with each error at most \(4\cdot2^{-k_n}\).  In particular, the zero-face certificate uses the face directions (2), not the refuted scalar subprior.

The same evaluator solves the finite rational action-grid program.  By the rational-grid primal-error lemma, its feasible optimizer is a total randomized estimator and satisfies (B) with an outward rational error bounded by the left side of (33).  This proves the attaining statement against every fixed schedule.

Define
\[
 j(N)=\max\{j\leq N:N_j\leq N\},
 \qquad E(N)=5\cdot2^{-j(N)}
 \tag{36}
\]
after enlarging its finitely many prefix values to cover the startup outputs.  The function in (36) is rational-valued, computable, and nonincreasing.  Since every fixed \(N_j\) is eventually passed, \(j(N)\to\infty\), so \(E(N)\to0\).  Monotonicity of (34), (33), and the three bounds following (35) proves (C) for every \(n\geq N\).  This supplies the required cross-sample certificate rather than inferring it from finite enumeration.

It remains to transfer the certificates to the unrestricted game.  By the face-robust orbit lemma, every outcome-independent, possibly dependent labeled design and every randomized estimator have Bayes risk at least
\(B_{n,k_n,\varepsilon_n^{\mathrm A}}^{\dagger,\mathrm A}\).  Since the three strata partition \(\mathcal R_{n,3}\), (A) and the exact definition of \(G\) give
\[
\begin{aligned}
n^{4/3}\left\{n^{-1}-B_{n,k_n,\varepsilon_n^{\mathrm A}}^{\dagger,\mathrm A}\right\}
&=\max_{r\in\mathcal R_{n,3}}
G_{n,k_n,\varepsilon_n^{\mathrm A}}^{\dagger,\mathrm A}(r)\\
&\leq\Lambda_{c^\dagger}
+\max\{e_{\mathrm{loc},n},e_{\mathrm{shell},n},e_{\mathrm{zero},n}\}.
\end{aligned} \tag{37}
\]
Maximum risk dominates Bayes risk, so the infimum in the risk-game definition and (37) give the upper bound on the scaled deficit.  The feasible procedure in (B) gives its lower bound.  The squeeze and (C) prove convergence to \(\Lambda_{c^\dagger}\).  Finally, the exact-primitives proposition gives \(\kappa(c^\dagger)=5/8\), and the Airy-benchmark definition gives
\(\Lambda_{c^\dagger}=C_A(5/8)^{2/3}\in(0,\infty)\).  This proves every assertion.
